Z||000000||Seanh||03-31-2001||03:27 PM||||I am going to redo my interior of my Fiero in two-tone gray vinyl. I want somthing similar to what Sluppy123 has done. I was wondering on a few things though. First off, has anyone covered the dash in vinyl? How difficult would this be to do? How do you do corners to make it look real good? And lastly, how does it hold up to heat and sunlight? I was also wondering if anyone has done the armrest's and upper portion of the door trim in vinyl and how it looks. I would like to do the top of it in ligher gray, and the bottem(now carpeted) in darker gray. How difficult is it to do the arm rests? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-31-2001||05:53 PM||||those factory armrests would be a real pita. Sewing would be required. If i really wanted to do something, id make new ones from scratch out of wood, pad it and cover it. I have a flat armrest running back from my door handle and going down at an angle to the back, it was ez to cover. Then I just made a strap to pull door shut. photo #11<A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556337" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556337</A>  <P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-31-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-31-2001).]||||reg||1
