Z||000006||Seanh||03-31-2001||09:07 PM||||Those all look great! That is excatly what I want to do with the shifter surround. I am going to cover it just like DXR_DAD did, and get a woodgrain overlay for the silver part, or maybe carbon fiber, haven't decided yet. How did you do the upper edge of the lower door panel? Did you cover the upper part of the panel? I will have to look over mine a little better and decide if I really need to cover the upper portion or not. I am still worried about the arm rest. I really like the look of the way rogergarrison did it, except the idea of a strap to close the door. I'm not crazy about that idea, I would rather have a solid handle or somthing. I am going to go down to an upholsty shop tomarrow and ask how much it would cost to have them sew and cover the factory armrest. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||03-31-2001||09:41 PM||||A thin strip of plastic was cut the shape of the the top egde and then the vinyl stretched over it and glued down then glued to the door panel = perfect edge.<BR>The upper part is stock. Trying to get the two tone, stock light gray & my light gray<BR>so I need to get somthing done to the dark gray on the top dash, maybe dye would be best or just a vinyl pad/cover??<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000008||sluppy123||03-31-2001||11:48 PM||||I don't know how difficult it would be to cover the dash or the arm rests, both have some complex curves. It would be very difficult to cover the entire dash with one solid piece of vinyl, with-out having a seam or a sewn edge. You would need a good quality glue and some really flexible vinyl.<P>DXR- where did you get the leather shift boot? Mr Mike? I ended up making my own, I cut the old one up to make a template, then sewed a new one. Wasn't to difficult, just had to recall some of those home economics classes.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered, Nitrous<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=37756786&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||DXR_DAD||03-31-2001||11:54 PM||||Sluppy I thought about making mine but I missed that day in class  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>Yes, I got the shift boot and ebrake boot from Mr.Mike||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||04-01-2001||12:40 AM||||What do you think I should do with the dash then? I am not the best at covering, and don't what to screw up my dash. I will talk to a shop Monday and see what they say. I really like the look and feel of vinyl. You guys would think this sounds a little over-kill, but pretty much the entire interion will be in vinyl. Console, ECM cover/glove box, shift boot, guage surrounds, even the little plate that covers the cigg. ligher. I am also going to look into doing the all the panels around the carpet edges and window edges in vinyl also. This should look pretty good though.||||reg||1
